      "rev_n_2_a5e355_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_a5e355_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_a5e355",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is correct in its logic but inefficient due to the nested loops, leading to a time complexity of O(n * (x + y)). We can optimize this by precomputing the minimum rain amounts for the x days before and y days after each day, which will allow us to check if a day is not so rainy in constant time. This optimization will reduce the time complexity to O(n).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_a5e355_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_01fd202917",
        "created_at": 1794531187.8877447
      },
      "rev_n_3_b5d4bd_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_b5d4bd_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_b5d4bd",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous implementation was in the range check for the suffix minimum. The condition `i + y < n` should be `i + y + 1 <= n` to ensure we don't access an index out of bounds. This oversight caused the function to miss the correct answer in some cases. Let's correct this and provide a brief explanation of the fix.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_b5d4bd_0",
